course: dictionary
lesson: 8675
title: Sedge: a wetland plant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A sedge is a grass-like plant. It grows in wet places such as marshes, ponds and riverbanks, so if a plant has wet feet, it might be a sedge.
explain: Here is a rhyme to tell sedges from other plants: «sedges have edges, rushes are round, grasses are hollow». Sedge stems are often triangular, so run your finger along one and feel the edges.
explain: Sedges matter in nature because they give shelter to insects and birds in wetland habitats. Lemmings are small rodents that eat grasses, moss and sedges. The list tells you that sedges are a kind of plant, just like grasses and moss.
fact: A sedge is a grass-like plant that grows in wet places.
fact: Sedges are found in marshes, ponds and riverbanks.
fact: Sedge stems are often triangular, which helps you tell them apart from rushes and grasses.
fact: «Sedge grass» and «sedge warbler» are phrases you may meet in science lessons.
fact: Context clue: in «eating grasses, moss and sedges», the list shows that sedges are plants, like grasses and moss.
exercise: «Lemmings are small rodents related to voles, living on the tundra and mountains of Scandinavia, Russia, Canada and Alaska, eating grasses, moss and sedges.» What is a sedge? | A small furry animal that eats grass | A type of rock found on the tundra | A tall tree on a mountain | *A grass-like plant that grows in wet places
exercise: Where is a sedge most likely to grow? | A kitchen shelf | A dry desert | *A riverbank | A hot, empty road
exercise: The rhyme says «sedges have edges, rushes are round». What shape are sedge stems often? | Round like a rush | Hollow like a grass stem | *Triangular
test: Which phrase names a bird that lives among sedges? | sedge grass | riverbank rush | *sedge warbler
test: What do sedges give to insects and birds in wetland habitats? | Sand | *Shelter | Oil | Ice
exam: In «eating grasses, moss and sedges», what kind of word is sedges most likely to be? | *A kind of plant | A kind of rock | A kind of cloud | A kind of animal
